Figure 2.7 lists a simple test program to verify that a computer supports virtual addresses.
The program has a single static variable; it updates the value of the variable, waits for a few
seconds, and then prints the location of the variable and its value.
 int staticVar = 0;    // a static variable 
 main() { 
     staticVar += 1; 

     // sleep causes the program to wait for x seconds 
     sleep(10); 
     printf ("Address: %x; Value: %d\n", &staticVar, staticVar); 
 } 

 Produces: 
